@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: how proveo puts a directory on PATH across shells, and how it takes it back off
' covers: internal/shell/shell.go
' covers: internal/shell/shell_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/setup.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/setup_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/uninstall.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/uninstall_test.go
'   the OTHER directory it writes . _spec/cmd/proveo/init-sbx-bootstrap.puml
'   the installer that calls setup  _spec/internal/cdn/distribution-update.puml
'   the wave that set these lines . _spec/_plans/output-readability.puml (R4)
'
' ── TWO BLOCKS, TWO MARKERS ────────────────────────────────────────────────
' `proveo setup` writes Marker for proveo's own bin dir; `proveo init` writes
' SbxMarker (SbxBlock) for the sbx prefix's bin dir. They are DISTINCT comments,
' because a shared one would claim that a line pointing at ~/.docker/sbx/bin
' puts "proveo on PATH". `proveo uninstall` strips an install.sh block or a
' Marker block whose PATH line names this root's bin dir, and either marker
' with no PATH line under it; another dir's block stays (~/go/bin's: FOUND 9
' makes two in one rc normal, the R4 review), and so does SbxMarker's, since
' sbx (~/.docker/sbx) stays installed after proveo leaves. uninstall.sh's
' bash fallback strips every Marker and SbxMarker block (KNOWN divergence,
' the installer's owner: the Go uninstall is right). Pinned by
' TestUninstallLeavesAnotherDirsSetupBlock and
' TestUninstallLeavesAnotherRootsInstallBlock.
'
' ── THE RC NAMES THE DIRECTORY, NOT A MARKER (R4, FOUND 9) ─────────────────
' AlreadyConfigured answers "does this rc name THIS directory". It used to
' accept setup's marker alone, so an rc holding a marker for another dir (an
' earlier `go install` proveo in ~/go/bin) read as configured and got no line.
' init asks the same question for the sbx prefix (rcAdds, ensureSbxOnPath),
' so both callers share it and its file write (appendRC). A dir under HOME
' also counts as $HOME/…, ${HOME}/… or ~/…: install.sh runs setup with the
' dir off PATH, which would otherwise repeat such a hand line (the R4 review).
' Only a PATH line counts (PATH, zsh's path, fish_add_path), and only with the
' dir as a whole entry: with the dir off PATH this check is the one gate, and
' a comment, an alias, another variable or ~/.proveo/binaries would leave a
' fresh install with no line. Pinned by TestAMentionOutsideAPathLineIsNotConfigured,
' TestAlreadyConfigured, TestAlreadyConfiguredReadsTheDirSpelledFromHome,
' TestSetupWritesThisDirsLineUnderAnotherDirsMarker and
' TestSetupReadsAnRcLineThatNamesTheDirFromHome.
'
' ── WHAT `proveo setup` PRINTS (R4 of _spec/_plans/output-readability.puml) ─
' No heading; ONE item, init's PATH item word for word. The checks run PATH
' first (critique must-fix 2: a head says "not on PATH" only after setup
' looked), then the shell, then the rc:
'   on PATH            ✓ ~/.proveo/bin — already on PATH          (any shell)
'   csh, tcsh          ⚠ ~/.proveo/bin — not on PATH, dim "add to ~/.cshrc:
'                      setenv PATH …"; exit 0, nothing written
'   unknown $SHELL     × ~/.proveo/bin — not on PATH, dim "$SHELL is not set"
'                      or "<name> is not a shell setup knows", dim "add it to
'                      PATH in your shell's startup file" (Windows: "your
'                      user PATH"); exit 1, so install.sh falls back
'   the rc names it    ⚠ ~/.proveo/bin — not on this shell's PATH, dim
'                      "~/.zshrc adds it; a new shell picks it up"
'   --print            ⚠ <dir> — not on PATH, dim "add to <rc>: <line>", both
'                      absolute (P5); the marker comment leaves the screen:
'                      uninstall strips the bare export line too
'   written            ✓ ~/.proveo/bin — added to PATH in ~/.zshrc, dim "a new
'                      shell picks it up"
'   rc not written     × ~/.zshrc — not written, the error dim, dim "add it
'                      yourself: <line>"; exit 1
' A × is the command's own item, Reported (exit 1, main prints nothing).
' "source <rc>" and the csh rule moved to `proveo setup --help`.
' Pinned by cmd/proveo/setup_test.go, one test per row.
'
' ── WHAT `proveo uninstall` PRINTS (R4) ────────────────────────────────────
' No heading. The question names each part it finds, from the checks the
' block uses: "› remove ~/.proveo, its PATH lines and the prompt kit? [y/N]"
' ("proveo's PATH lines" with no root; none found asks nothing). Dangerf's
' red "this removes proveo from <root>" left (P9). A "n" is "⚠ uninstall —
' cancelled", exit 0. No terminal and no --yes: "× proveo — not uninstalled",
' dim "`proveo uninstall --yes` uninstalls it without asking" (NO TTY);
' PROVEO_UNINSTALL_ASSUME_YES moved to --yes's help.
' Then ONE Facts block of what left, error role, a fact only for a removal
' that succeeded (the operator, "by what left"):
'   root    ~/.proveo
'   path    each rc a PATH line left, stacked
'   prompt  the kit's rc and starship config, and its starship binary when
'           the root fact does not already cover it
'   font    FiraCode Nerd Font, dim "3 files in ~/Library/Fonts" (init's)
' Each removal that failed is a ⚠ item ("~/.bashrc — PATH line not removed",
' "~/.config/starship.toml — proveo segment not removed", the error dim);
' FOUND 3 and 4 printed "removed" and ✓ over them. Then what proveo's own
' records say stays (the operator, "⚠ each, with its fix"; no sbx,
' launchctl or systemctl call):
'   ⚠ ~/go/bin/proveo — still on PATH        (exec.LookPath, read-only)
'   ⚠ <exe> — not removed, dim "outside ~/.proveo"   (the running binary)
'   ⚠ schedule tick — still registered, dim schedule.RemoveCommand:
'     "launchctl bootout gui/<uid>/io.proveo.schedule; rm ~/Library/…plist"
'     or "systemctl --user disable --now proveo-schedule.timer; rm …"
'   ⚠ <name> — kept, its output only inside   (each kept entry; no command:
'     `proveo rm` leaves with proveo, and a deleting sbx command was ruled out)
' ONE closing line: "✓ proveo — uninstalled", or "⚠ proveo — uninstalled; N
' left" when N ⚠ items print ("nothing removed" when a part was found and
' none went; "nothing to remove" when none was found). A root that stays
' closes on × and exits 1: "~ — not removed", dim "an unsafe install root",
' or "~/.proveo — not fully removed", the RemoveAll error dim.
' "hash -r" and the state root moved to `proveo uninstall --help`.
' Pinned by cmd/proveo/uninstall_test.go and init_prompt_test.go
' TestUninstallTakesThePromptKitOutAndLeavesTheOperatorsConfig.
'
' ── KNOWN, NOT FIXED (R4 allowed no other behaviour change) ────────────────
' FOUND 5: the unsafe-root check runs after the rc strips and the prompt
' kit's undo, so PROVEO_INSTALL_ROOT=$HOME leaves a half-uninstalled host;
' the guard stays inside removeInstallRoot. A typo'd root (~/Documents) or a
' relative one is removed (critique d9). FOUND 10: with HOME unset, setup
' resolves the rc against the working directory. `proveo setup` run by hand
' with the dir on this shell's PATH only by an `export` still answers
' "already on PATH" and writes nothing (install.sh no longer reaches it: it
' runs setup with the dir off PATH). The question goes to
' stderr and IsStdinTTY alone gates it, so `proveo uninstall 2>log` waits
' unseen (d8). Windows: uninstall cannot remove the running proveo.exe (a ×,
' "not fully removed") and leaves install.ps1's user PATH entry.
' [Inference] "its output only inside" overstates for a kept mounted-checkout
' sandbox; the kept entry does not record the mode.
title `proveo setup` — cross-shell PATH wiring

actor "Consumer" as USER

node "Consumer host" as HOST <<host>> {
  component "dist/install.sh\n(hands off, else writes its block)" as INSTALL <<app>>
  component "cmd/proveo setup" as CMD <<app>>
  component "internal/shell\nDetect · RCFile · PathLine\nExportLine · AlreadyConfigured" as SH <<app>>
  database "rc file\n.bashrc/.bash_profile · .zshrc\nconfig.fish · .profile" as RC <<db>>
  component "proveo binary dir\n(GOPATH/bin or install dir)" as BIN <<app>>
}

USER ARROW_MAIN INSTALL
INSTALL ARROW_MAIN CMD : after install
USER ARROW_OPTIONAL CMD : " ""proveo setup"" "
CMD ARROW_MAIN SH : " ""Detect($SHELL)"" "
SH ARROW_MAIN SH : " ""RCFile(goos, home)"" "
SH ARROW_OPTIONAL RC : checks ""AlreadyConfigured(content, binDir)""\nno-op when the rc names the dir
SH ARROW_MAIN RC : appends ""PathLine(binDir)""
RC ARROW_MAIN BIN : next login shell resolves ""proveo""

note right of SH
  **Syntax differs per shell, so it is data, not a
  template.** bash/zsh export ""PATH=…:$PATH""; fish uses
  ""set -gx PATH … $PATH""; csh-family uses ""setenv"".
  ""Supported"" marks shells proveo can write for —
  an unrecognized ""$SHELL"" is reported, never guessed at.

  **macOS bash takes ""~/.bash_profile"", Linux bash takes
  ""~/.bashrc""** — a login-shell difference that silently
  no-ops if you pick wrong.

  ""AlreadyConfigured"" makes the command idempotent: run
  it twice and the rc file gains one line, not two.
end note
note bottom of SH
  A typed, tested resolver rather than a regex over an rc file: the shells
  differ in which file is read for a login versus an interactive session,
  and an unparsed edit to the wrong one silently fails to take effect.
end note


@enduml
